hadiths[165]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4291","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Salam bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah, on the authority of my father Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “that he hated the forms of horses.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4292","Qutayba bin Saeed and Muhammad bin Mansour reported, and the wording is his. He said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “Bad badness is found in three things: the woman, the horse, and the house.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4293","And Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, a reading from him while I was listening. And the wording is for him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik reported, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Hamza and Salem, the sons of Abdullah bin Omar, On the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Bad badness is in the house, the woman, and the horse.”"
"4294","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Khalid told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “If bad luck is found in anything, it is in a woman, a woman, or a horse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4295","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Al-Nadr reported, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Anas, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Abu Al-Tayyah told me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “ Blessing is in the horses’ forelocks.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4296","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Zur’ah bin Amr bin Jarir, On the authority of Jarir, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, twisting the forelock of a horse between his two fingers, and saying: The horses are tied at their forelocks.” “Goodness will last until the Day of Resurrection, reward and spoils.”"
"4297","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The horses are in their forelocks.” goodness until the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4298","Muhammad ibn al-Ala reported, he said: Ibn Idris reported, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Urwa al-Bariqi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he said: “Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4299","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Urwa bin Abu Al-Jaad, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection, reward and spoils.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4300","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Urwa, He said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Horses have reward and spoils tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4301","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Abd al-Rahman told us, saying: Shu`bah told us, saying: Husayn and Abdullah bin Abi al-Safar told me, that they heard Al-Sha’abi narrates, on the authority of Urwa bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “Horses will have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of The Resurrection is the reward and the spoils.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4302","Al-Hasan bin Ismail bin Suleiman reported, he said: Issa bin Yunus reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, he said: Abu Salam told me Al-Dimashqi, on the authority of Khaled bin Zaid Al-Juhani, said: “Uqba bin Amir used to pass by me, and he said: O Khaled, take us out of Ram, and when he One day I was late for him, and he said: O Khaled, come and I will tell you what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me. So I went to him, and he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, with one arrow, God admits three people into Paradise. Its maker expects goodness in his making. And the one who shoots it, and the one who throws it, and shoot and ride, and that you shoot is more beloved to me than that you ride, and there is no amusement except in three things: disciplining a man. His horse, his playing with his wife, his shooting with his bow, and the like. And whoever abandons archery after teaching him that he wanted it, it is a blessing. He disbelieved in it, or he said: He disbelieved in it.”"
"4303","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Ibn Zurayr, on the authority of Ali bin Abi A student said: “A mule was given to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he rode it. Ali said: If we had carried the donkeys on the horses, they would have been We have something like this. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Only those who do not know do that."
"4304","Humayd ibn Masada narrated, saying: Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Jahdham, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Abbas, he said: “I was with Ibn Abbas, and a man asked him: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite during the noon and afternoon prayers? He said: No. He said: Perhaps he used to recite during the noon and afternoon prayers. Himself? He said: This is a hermaphrodite that is worse than the first. Indeed, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is a servant to whom God commanded him to do something, and he conveyed it to him. By God, he did not The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, singled us out for something, to the exclusion of others, except for three: He commanded us to perform ablution properly, and not to eat from charity. And do not ride donkeys on horses.”"
"4305","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Talha bin Abi Saeed narrated to me, that Saeed Al-Maqbari narrated to him, on the authority of my father Huraira, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever keeps a horse in the path of God out of faith in God and in confirmation of God’s promise has “His satiety and his drinking, and his urine and his dung, will be good deeds in his scale on the Day of Resurrection.”"
"4306","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported a reading of it, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He raced among the horses that were free from loss, and their duration was the time of farewell, and he raced among the horses that did not. It is led from the second to the Mosque of Banu Zurayk,” and that Abdullah was among those who preceded it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4307","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raced between horses.” He sends it from Al-Hafiyah, and its duration was Thaniyat Al-Wadaa, and it raced between the horses that were not hammed, and its duration was from Thaniyat to Masjid. \Bani Zurayq\"""""
"4308","Ismail bin Masoud reported, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Abi Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no precedence except with a blade, a hoof, or a shoe.”"
"4309","Saeed bin Abdul Rahman reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Abi Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no precedence except with a blade, a shoe, or a hoof.”"
"4310","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ja’far, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd Al-Rahman, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, on the authority of Abu Abdullah, the client of Al-Janda’iyyin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: “It is not permissible to race unless one is wearing socks or hoofer (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4311","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Khalid, who said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a she-camel called A Bedouin woman cannot be outpaced, so a Bedouin came sitting on his feet, and he overtook them and treated the Muslims with hardship. When he saw what was on their faces, they said: O Messenger of God, Al-‘Udhaba preceded him in saying: “Indeed, it is a duty of God that nothing of the world should be raised except what He places.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4312","Imran bin Musa reported, saying: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Hakam, a client of Banu Laith, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no precedence unless one is wearing a hoof or sandals.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4313","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ reported, saying: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Humaid told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “There is no impurity, no impurity, and no discord in Islam, and whoever plunders is not one of us.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4314","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Qaza’ah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no impurity, no impurity, and no shigra in Islam.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4315","Amr bin Uthman bin Saeed bin Kathir told me, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Shu`bah told me, he said: Humaid al-Taweel told me, on the authority of Anas bin Malik said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, raced against an Arab, and he preceded him, and it was as if the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” They found it within themselves about that, so he said: It is a duty upon God that nothing in this world should elevate itself unless God has placed it."
"4316","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of his grandfather, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, struck in the year of Khaybar Al-Zubayr bin Al-Awwam has four shares, one share goes to Al-Zubayr, and one share goes to a relative of Safiyya bint Abdul Muttalib, mother of Al-Zubayr. And two arrows for the horse.”"
"4317","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Othman bin Omar told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Yazid bin Hurmuz, “that Najda When Al-Haruri came out of the strife of Ibn Al-Zubayr, he sent to Ibn Abbas asking him about the arrow of a relative. Who do you think it is for? He said: Ours for a relative The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, apportioned it to us. Omar had presented something to us that we had seen without actually having it. But we refused to accept it, and the one who offered it to them was that he would help and pay for their debtors and give to the poor of them, and he refused to add anything to them. \that\"""""
"4318","Amr bin Ali reported, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, and Muhammad bin Ali, on the authority of Yazid bin Hormuz said: “Najda wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him: Whose kin’s arrow is it for? Yazid bin Hurmuz said: I wrote a letter. Ibn Abbas to Najda, I wrote to him: You wrote to ask me about the share of a relative, whose share is it for us, the Ahl al-Bayt, and it was? Omar invited us to marry him and serve our family, and pay off our debts from him, but we refused except for him to hand him over to us, and he refused to do that. So we left him on it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4319","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Hakam reported, saying: Shuaib ibn Yahya told us, saying: Nafi` ibn Yazid told us, on the authority of Yunus ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyib told me, “Jubayr bin Mut’im told him that he and Uthman bin Affan came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They were speaking to him about what he had divided from the fifth of Khaybar between Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf. They said: O Messenger of God, you have divided To our brothers Banu al-Muttalib ibn Abd Manaf, and you did not give us anything and our kinship is like their kinship, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: And peace be upon him: It is only the sons of Hashim, and the demand is one. Jubayr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not swear to the sons of Abd Shams, nor did Banu Nawfal will get something of that fifth, just as he divided it among Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib.”"
"4320","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna reported, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq reported, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Jubayr ibn Mut’im. He said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided the shares of the kin between Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib, I and Othman bin Affan went to him. So we said: O Messenger of God, these are Banu Hashim. Their virtue cannot be denied due to your position in which God has placed you among them. Have you seen the Banu al-Muttalib? You gave them and withheld us, but we and they are in a position with you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: They did not separate from me during the pre-Islamic era. And there is no Islam. Banu Hashim and Banu al-Muttalib are one and the same thing. He interlaced his fingers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4321","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith narrated, saying: Mahboub, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari narrated, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ayyash, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Salam, on the authority of Abu Umamah al-Bahili, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: “The Prophet took On the day of Hunayn, may God bless him and grant him peace, he and a camel’s camel’s side, and he said: O people, it is not permissible for me of what God has bestowed on you to the extent of this, except The fifth, and the fifth will be returned to you.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Salam’s name is Mumtur, and Abu Umamah’s name is Siddi ibn Ajlan. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4322","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to a camel and took from its hump a camel between his two fingers, then he said: Here, “I do not have any of the fay’, nor this, except the fifth, and the fifth will be returned to you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4323","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin Al-Hadathan, on the authority of Omar, he said: “It was The wealth of Banu al-Nadir was from what God gave to His Messenger, and the Muslims did not pay him horses or riders, so he used to spend on himself from it as food. A year, and for what remained he put on his armor and weapons as equipment in the path of God.”"
"4324","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith reported, saying: Mahboub told us, saying: Abu Ishaq reported, on the authority of Shuaib bin Abi Hamza, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, “Fatima sent to Abu Bakr asking him for her inheritance from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he was safe from his charity, and from what he left behind, and from the fifth of Khaybar. Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: We do not inherit what we leave behind. \charity\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4325","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith reported, saying: Mahboub told us, saying: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Ata’, “In his saying, ‘Whatever thing you gain, a fifth of it belongs to God and to the Messenger.’ He said: ‘One-fifth belongs to God and one-fifth to His Messenger,’” he said. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is one. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to carry from it, give from it, place it wherever he wished, and do with it whatever he wished.”"
"4326","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith narrated, saying: Mahboub bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari narrated, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Qays. Ibn Muslim, I asked Al-Hassan Ibn Muhammad about the words of God Almighty: And know that whatever thing you gain, a fifth of it belongs to God. He said: “ This is the key to his speech. To God belongs this world and the hereafter. He said: They disagreed about these two arrows after the death of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Messenger, and the share of a relative. Someone said: The Messenger’s share is for the caliph after him, and someone said: The share of a relative is for the kinship of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and someone said: The arrow of a relative, related to the caliph’s kinship. So their minds agreed that they put these two arrows in the horses. And the waiting period in the path of God, and that included the caliphate of Abu Bakr and Omar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4327","Amr bin Yahya reported, saying: Mahboub told us, saying: Abu Ishaq reported, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, he said: I asked Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, Concerning this verse: And know that whatever thing you gain, a fifth of it belongs to God. He said: I said: How much of the fifth did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, have? He said: One-fifth. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4328","Amr bin Yahya reported, saying: Mahboub told us, saying: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, he said: Al-Sha’bi was asked about the share of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted his successor and said: “As for the arrow of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, a man from among the Muslims shot them. \He willed\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4329","Amr bin Yahya bin Al-Harith reported, saying: Mahboub told us, saying: Abu Ishaq reported, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Shakhir, He said: “While I was with a farmer in Al-Mirabad, a man entered with a piece of leather and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote this to me. Is it Is there anyone among you who is reading? I said: I am reading, and then it says: From Muhammad to Banu Zuhair bin Qais: If they bear witness that there is no god but Allah, And that Muhammad is the Messenger of God, and they dispersed from the polytheists, and gave a fifth of their spoils, and the arrows of the Prophet and his successors, for they are safe in the security of God. and His Messenger.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4330","Amr bin Yahya reported, saying: Mahboub told us, saying: Abu Ishaq reported, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: “The fifth that belongs to God For the Messenger, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his relatives did not eat any of the charity, so it was for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “One-fifth of a fifth, and the same for a relative, and the same for orphans, the same for the needy, and the same for the wayfarer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4331","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail, who is the son of Aliyah, informed us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Malik bin Aws bin The two hadiths, he said: “Al-Abbas and Ali came to Omar to dispute, and Al-Abbas said: Arbitrate between me and this man. Then the people said: Separate between them. So Omar said: I will not separate between them, as they knew that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “We will not inherit anything, as long as we leave it as charity.” He said: Then Al-Zuhri said: Its custodian is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took from it the sustenance of his family and all his way was the way of money. Then its custodian is Abu Bakr. After him, then I took charge of it after Abu Bakr, and I did to it what he had done, then they came to me and asked me to hand it over to them on the condition that they would take over it. With the one with which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, appointed her to her, and the one with which Abu Bakr appointed her to her, and I appointed her to do so, so I handed it over to them. I took their covenants accordingly, then this man came to me saying: “Give me an oath from my brother’s son,” and this one says: “Give me my share from my wife.” If they wish, I can hand it over to them with what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, assigned it to me, and what Abu Bakr assigned it to me, and with which I appointed it. With it, I will hand it over to them, and if they come, it will be sufficient for them. Then he said: And know that whatever thing you spoil, a fifth of it is for God and for the Messenger and what Relatives, orphans, the needy, and the wayfarer. This verse is for them: Charities are only for the poor and needy and those who work to give them. And whose hearts will be reconciled, and for the freeing of slaves and the debtors, and in the path of God and the wayfarer. This is for these: And what God has fulfilled from His Messenger of them, then what Did you send horses or riders to it? Al-Zuhri said: This is for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, specifically, Arab villages: Fadak and so on. Likewise, whatever God bestows upon His Messenger from the people of the villages belongs to God and to the Messenger and to relatives and orphans and the needy and the wayfarer, and to the poor. The immigrants who were expelled from their homes and their property, and those who settled in the land and the faith before them, and those who came after them So this verse understood the people, and not one of the Muslims remained who did not have a right to this money, or he said a share, except for some of those whom you possess. One of your slaves, and if I live, God willing, every Muslim will be given his due, or he said: his share."
"4332","Sulayman bin Salam Al-Balkhi told us, trustworthy, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Ibn Muslim On the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “Whoever sees the crescent of Dhul-Hijjah and wants to sacrifice, He must not take any of his hair or his nails until he sacrifices.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4333","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth informed us, he said: Khaled bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Ibn Abu Hilal, on the authority of Amr bin Muslim, that he said: Ibn al-Musayyab informed me that Umm Salamah was the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, I told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wants to make a sacrifice should not trim his nails, and should not shave any of his hair.” On the first ten days of Dhul-Hijjah, Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Amr bin Muslim bin Ammar bin Ukaymah. There was disagreement about his name, so it was said: Omar, It was said: Amr, and he is a civilian (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4334","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told me. Ibn Awf, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “When the first ten days have begun, and one of you wants to He sacrifices, but does not touch any of his hair or skin.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4335","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub told me, and he mentioned others, on the authority of Ayyash Ibn Abbas Al-Qatabani, on the authority of Issa Ibn Hilal Al-Sadfi, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr Ibn Al-Aas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said To a man: “I was ordered to celebrate the Day of Sacrifice as a holiday that God Almighty has made for this nation. The man said: What do you think? If I find nothing but an unmarried female, should I sacrifice it?” With it? He said: No, but if you trim your hair, trim your nails, trim your mustache, and shave your pubic hair, that is the completion of your sacrifice before God. \Glory be to Him\"""""
"4336","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam informed us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Al-Layth, on the authority of Kathir bin Farqad, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah He told him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to slaughter or sacrifice in the prayer place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4337","Ali bin Othman Al-Nufaili Al-Harrani told us, he said: Saeed bin Issa told us, he said: Al-Mufaddal bin Fadalah told us, he said: Abdullah told me Ibn Sulaiman, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Omar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered the Day of Eid al-Adha in Medina. He said: And if he did not slaughter, he slaughtered it in the prayer place."
"4338","Hanad bin Al-Sirri told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Jundub bin Sufyan, who said: “I witnessed the Eid al-Adha with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led the people in prayer. When he finished the prayer, he saw sheep that had been slaughtered, so he said: Whoever slaughters before the prayer, let him slaughter a sheep. in its place, and whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter in the name of God Almighty.”"
"4339","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman, the client of Banu Asad, on the authority of Ubay Al-Dahhak Ubaid bin Fayrouz, a client of Banu Shayban, said: I said to Al-Baraa, “Tell me about what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade regarding sacrifices. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up while my hand was shorter than his hand, and he said: Four things that cannot be distinguished: the one-eyed woman whose one-eyed one is clearly visible, and the sick woman. Its sickness is clearly evident, and the lame is clearly visible, and the broken one is not cleansed. I said: I hate for there to be deficiency in the century, and for There will be a deficiency in the tooth. He said: And whatever you dislike, leave it, and do not forbid it to anyone."
"4340","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far, Abu Dawud, Yahya, Abdul Rahman, Ibn Abi Adi, and Abu Al-Walid, they said: Shu`bah told us, he said: I heard Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I heard Ubaid bin Fayrouz, he said: I told Al-Baraa bin A single man told me about the sacrifices that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, disliked or forbade. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He said like this with his hand, and my hand is shorter than the hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There are four things that are not sufficient for sacrificial animals: the one-eyed woman whose one-eyedness is clearly evident, And the sick woman whose illness is clearly evident, and the lame woman whose limbs are clearly evident, and the broken woman who cannot be cleaned. He said: I hate for there to be a deficiency in The horn and the ear. He said: Whatever of it you dislike, leave it and do not forbid it to anyone. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4341","Suleiman bin Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith and Al-Layth bin Saad told me, and he mentioned another and introduced it, Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman told them, on the authority of Ubaid bin Fayrouz, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Azib, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello and pointed with his fingers, and my fingers are shorter than the fingers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he pointed with his finger and said: “No.” It is permissible for victims to include a one-eyed woman whose defect is clear, a lame woman whose lameness is clear, a sick woman whose illness is clearly evident, and a lame woman who cannot be cleaned.”"
"4342","Muhammad ibn Adam informed me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahim, who is the son of Sulaiman, on the authority of Zakaria ibn Abi Zaida, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shurayh ibn Al-Numan, on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to look out for the eye and the ear and not to sacrifice.” “By confrontation, nor deliberation, nor deceit, nor clumsiness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4343","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Shurayh bin Al-Numan: Abu Ishaq said: He was a man who told the truth on the authority of Ali, may God be pleased with him. He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to “We should seek out the eye and the ear, and we will not sacrifice one who is one-eyed, one who meets, one who is scheming, one who is intelligent, or one who is clumsy.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4344","Ahmad ibn Nasih al-Masisi informed us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Shurayh ibn al-Nu’man, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade us to sacrifice by facing each other, or facing each other, or \Straight"," or clumsy"," or stumpy.\"""""
"4345","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Shuja’ bin Al-Walid told us, he said: Ziyad bin Khaythamah told me, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Shuraih ibn al-Numan, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Talib, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “A sacrifice is not to be made in return, nor \Neither arrogant"," nor clumsy"," nor one-eyed.\"""""
"4346","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, that Salamah, who was Ibn Kuhayl, told him, he said: I heard Hajiya bin Adiy, saying: I heard Ali saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to look out with the eye and the ear.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4347","Humayd ibn Masada informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, who is Ibn Habib, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Jari ibn Kulayb, he said: I heard Ali, he says: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade sacrificing a horned animal.” I mentioned that to Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and he said: Yes. The largest amount is half or more than that."
"4348","Abu Dawud told us, Al-Hasan told us, and he is the son of Muhammad bin Ayn Al-Harrani, and Abu Ja’far, meaning Ibn Nufail Al-Nufaili, told us: He told us Zuhayr, who said: Abu Al-Zubayr told us, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not slaughter anything except a Sunnah animal unless it is difficult for you.” Then slaughter a lump of sheep.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4349","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, “that The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave him sheep to divide among his companions, so there were only goats left. He mentioned it to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: \Sacrifice him yourself\"""""
"4350","Yahya bin Durst told us, he said: Abu Ismail, who is Al-Qannad, and his name is Ibrahim bin Abdul-Malik told us, he said: Yahya told us He is Ibn Abi Kathir. He said: Ba’ja bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore Among his companions there were sacrifices, and a lump became mine, so I said: O Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a lump became mine, and he said: Sacrifice it.”"
"4351","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ba’ja bin Abdullah Al-Juhani, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, divided among his companions my sacrifices, and a stump struck me, so I said: Oh The Messenger of God was struck by a stump, and he said: Sacrifice it.”"
"4352","Suleiman bin Dawud informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr informed me, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Muadh bin Abdullah bin Khubayb, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, said: “We sacrificed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a leg of sheep.”"
"4353","Hanad bin Al-Sari told us in his hadith, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, who said: “We were on a journey, and he attended Al-Adha. So the man from us began to buy the musannah in two or three lumps, and a man from Muzainah said to us: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in He traveled on a journey, and this day arrived, and the man asked for the old woman in two or three jum’ahs. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The jum’ah He repays what the second repays.”"
"4354","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, he said: I heard my father talking, on the authority of A man said: “We were with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, two days before Eid al-Adha, giving the two juz’ahs by the second, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And he said: “The trunk does what the tuck does.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4355","Ishaq bin Ibrahim bin Rahawayh told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz, who is Ibn al-Ashab, on the authority of Anas, “that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to sacrifice two rams. Anas said: I will sacrifice two rams."
"4356","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed And he greeted with two salted rams.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4357","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed With two salted rams, with their horns, which he killed with his own hand, and he named him and said “Allahu Akbar” and put his foot on their sides.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4358","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed us on the day of Eid al-Adha, and he went down to two salty rams and slaughtered them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4359","Humayd ibn Masada informed us in his hadith, on the authority of Yazid ibn Zuray’, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Tomorrow, on the authority of his father, he said: “Then he went away, as if he meant the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to two salted rams, and he slaughtered them on the day of The sacrifice, and a lump of sheep, which he divided among us. “Abridged.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4360","Abdullah bin Saeed Abu Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, he said: Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Saeed He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed a ram with two horns and a camel that walks in darkness, eats in darkness, and looks in darkness.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4361","Ahmad bin Abdullah bin Al-Hakam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told us, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah bin Rafi’, on the authority of his grandfather Rafi’ bin Khadij, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to make “Dividing the spoils into ten sheep for a camel.” Shu’bah said: The greatest thing I know is that I heard it from Sa’id bin Masruq, and Sufyan told me about it. About him, and God Almighty knows best (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4362","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rizmah bin Ghazwan told us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Hussein, meaning Ibn Waqid, on the authority of Alba bin Ahmar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he prepared the sacrifice.” So we shared the camel for ten and the cow for seven.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4363","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “We used to enjoy ourselves with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, so we slaughter the cow for seven, and we share in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4364","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Yahya, and Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Burdah bin Niyar, that he slaughtered before the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to do so. He said: “I have a large she-camel that is dearer to me than two old ones.” He said: “Slaughter it,” according to the hadith of Ubayd Allah. He said: I do not find Except a lump, so he ordered him to slaughter it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4365","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Jundub bin Sufyan, he said: “We sacrificed with... The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came one day and saw that people had slaughtered their victims before the prayer. When he left, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw them. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said that they slaughtered before the prayer, and he said: Whoever slaughters before the prayer, let him slaughter another in its place, and whoever did not slaughter until... We prayed, so let him slaughter in the name of God Almighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4366","Hanad bin Al-Sirri informed us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: My father informed us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, He said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind informed us, on the authority of Aamer al-Sha’bi, on the authority of al-Bara’ ibn Aazib. One of them mentioned what the other did not mention. He said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up on the Day of Eid al-Adha and said: Whoever faces our qiblah, prays our prayers, and observes our rituals, should not slaughter until he has prayed. Then my uncle got up and said: O Messenger of God, I hastened my sacrifice in order to feed my family and my household, or my family and neighbors, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him: Prepare another slaughter. He said: I have a milk she-camel, which is dearer to me than two meat sheep. He said: Slay it, for it is better. “I will forget you, and do not make up for anyone after you.”"
"4367","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib, he said: “We addressed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Sacrifice after the prayer, then he said: Whoever prays our prayers and performs our rituals has fulfilled the rituals, and whoever performs your rituals Before prayer, that was a sheep of meat. Abu Burdah said: O Messenger of God, by God, we were silent before I went out to pray, and I knew that Today is a day of eating and drinking, so I was in a hurry and ate and fed my family and neighbors. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: That is a sheep. Meat. He said: I have a young she-camel that is better than two lambs. Will you be sufficient for me? He said: Yes, and you will not be sufficient for anyone after you."
"4368","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said On the Day of Sacrifice, peace be upon him: “Whoever slaughtered before the prayer, let him prepare it.” Then a man stood up and said: O Messenger of God, this is a day in which it is desired. Meat, so he mentioned a sheep from his neighbors, as if the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, had believed him. He said: I have a goat that is more beloved to me than two meat sheep. He granted him permission, and I do not know whether his permission extended to anyone else or not. Then he went back to two rams and slaughtered them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4369","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Safwan, “that he afflicted He killed two rabbits and did not find any iron with which to slaughter them, so he slaughtered them with a claw. He came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I I hunted two rabbits and did not find any iron to slaughter them with, so I slaughtered them with a cucumber. Should I eat? He said: “Eat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4370","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jaafar, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Hadir bin Al-Muhajir Al-Bahili told us, he said: I heard Suleiman bin Yassar narrated, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, “A wolf bit a sheep, so they slaughtered it with a sheep, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted \in eating it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4371","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala and Ismail bin Masoud told us, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Ibn Qatari His name is Al-Marri, on the authority of Adi bin Hatim, who said: “I said: O Messenger of God, I am sending my dog to take the game, but I cannot find anything to slaughter it with. So slaughter it with a claw and a stick. He said: Spill the blood as you wish, and mention the name of God Almighty. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4372","Muhammad bin Muammar told me, he said: Hibban bin Hilal told us, he said: Jarir bin Hazim told us, he said: Ayyub told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, So I met Zayd bin Aslam, and he told me on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, who said: “A man from the Ansar had a she-camel grazing in... Before Uhud, he presented it to her and stabbed it with a stake. I said to Zaid: A stake of wood or iron? He said: No, but of wood. So he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and asked him, so he ordered him to eat it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4373","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of Rafi’ Bin Khadij, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whenever blood flows and the name of God is mentioned, eat it only with the tooth or fingernail.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4374","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, he said: “I said: O Messenger of God, we will meet the enemy tomorrow and we will not have a sharpshooter with us. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: What a stream of blood.” And mention the name of God Almighty, so eat as long as it is not tooth or fingernail, and I will tell you about that. As for the tooth, it is a bone, and as for the nail, it is long. \Abyssinia\"""""
"4375","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, he said: Two of them I memorized from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Indeed, God has prescribed goodness over all things, so when you kill, do good.” Killers, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let each one of you sharpen his blade, and let his slaughtered animal rest.”"
"4376","Issa bin Ahmad Al-Balkhi Al-Asqalani told us: Asqalan Balkh, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Sufyan told me, that Hisham bin Urwah told him, on the authority of Fatima bint Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abu Bakr, who said: “We slaughtered a horse at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, so we ate it.”"
"4377","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja’far, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Hadir bin Al-Muhajir Al-Bahili, he said: I heard Sulaiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, “A wolf bitten a sheep, so they slaughtered it with a sheep, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave permission for it.” \eat it\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4378","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu al-Ashra’, on the authority of his father, he said: “I said: O Messenger of God, is the zakat only required for the throat and the lobe? He said: If you had stabbed her in the thigh, I would have sufficed for you.”"
"4379","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of Rafi’ He said: “I said: O Messenger of God, we will meet the enemy tomorrow, and we have no range.” He said: As long as blood flows and the name of God Almighty is mentioned, then eat everything except the tooth. And victory, he said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was plundered, and a camel ran down and a man shot it with an arrow, and he caught it, and said: Indeed, for these blessings Or he said: Camels are as wild as wild animals, so whatever of them overwhelms you, do to them in the same way."
"4380","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah On the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, he said: “I said: O Messenger of God, we will meet the enemy tomorrow, and we do not have a range of weapons with us.” He said: “How much blood will flow.” And he mentioned the name of God Almighty. Glory be to Him, each is not the tooth and the nail, and I will tell you: As for the tooth, it is a bone, and as for the nail, it is the extent of the Ethiopian, and we have been afflicted with the plunder of camels or sheep. Then a camel ran out of it, and a man shot it with an arrow and caught it. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: These camels have animals like animals. The beast, so if any of it overtakes you, do likewise to it.”"
"4381","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid al-Hudha’, On the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Asma al-Rahbi, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He says: “Indeed, God Almighty has prescribed goodness for everything, so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well.” And let one of you sacrifice his blade when he slaughters it, and let him sacrifice his slaughtered animal.”"
"4382","Al-Hussein bin Harith Abu Ammar informed us, he said: Jarir informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Ihsan is prescribed over all things, so if you kill So be good killers, and when you slaughter, then slaughter well, and let each one of you sharpen his blade and let his sacrifice rest.”"
"4383","Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, said: I learned two things from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “Indeed, God Almighty has written goodness upon Everything, so when you kill, kill well, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, and let each one of you sharpen his blade and let him go. \His sacrifice\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4384","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: Khalid told us, and Abdullah bin told us Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qilaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Shaddad bin Aws, he said: “Two things I learned from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Indeed, God Almighty has prescribed goodness over all things, so if you kill So be good killers, and when you slaughter, slaughter well, so that one of you may sharpen his blade, and let his sacrifice be comfortable.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4385","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Qatada told me, he said: I heard Anas, he said: “He sacrificed The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with two salty rams with two horns, saying “Allahu Akbar” and saying “Bismin’, and I saw him slaughtering them with his hand, placing them on They were greeted by him. I said: Did you hear it from him? He said: Yes?"
"4386","Ahmad ibn Nasih al-Musaysi told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Anas ibn Malik told us, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sacrificing two horned, salty rams, and he was saying his name and saying “Allahu Akbar” and I saw him slaughtering them with his own hand. placing his foot on their sides.”"
"4387","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar Al-Kufi told us, he said: Mus’ab bin Al-Miqdam told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, on the authority of Shu’bah, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “I saw him, meaning the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, slaughtering them with his hand, placing his foot on their sides, calling the name. “And he pronounces the takbir with two salty rams with two horns.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4388","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, he said: Sa’id told us, he said: Qatada told us, that Anas bin Malik He told them, “The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sacrificed two rams with salty horns. He stepped on their skins, slaughtered them, and gave the name, And he says “Allahu Akbar.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4389","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin informed us of a reading about it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim. He said: Malik told me, on the authority of Jafar bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered some camel with his hand, and he slaughtered \Some of them are different.\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4390","Qutaibah and Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asma She said: “We slaughtered a horse at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we ate it.” Qutaibah said in his hadith: So we ate its meat. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4391","Muhammad bin Adam Al-Masisi told me, he said: Abdah bin Sulaiman Kufi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asmaa, she said: “We slaughtered a horse during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while we were in Medina, and we ate it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4392","Qutaibah told us, he said: Yahya, who is Ibn Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, told us, on the authority of Ibn Hayyan, meaning Mansour, on the authority of Aamir bin And three, he said: “A man asked Ali, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, confide anything to you rather than to other people? Ali became angry until he turned red. He turned his face and said: He did not confide anything to me other than the people except that he spoke to me four words while I was at home, so he said: May God curse whoever curses. His father, and may God curse whoever slaughters for other than God, and may God curse whoever shelters an innovator, and may God curse whoever changes the light of the earth.”"
"4393","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade eating sacrificial meat after three days."
"4394","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, on the authority of Ghandar, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Muammar told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Abu Ubaid A servant of Ibn Awf, he said: “I witnessed Ali bin Abi Talib, may God honor his face, on the day of Eid, he began to pray before the sermon, then he prayed without... Adhan or Iqamah, then he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbidding anyone from abstaining from his ritual rituals for more than three days.”"
"4395","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Ya’qub told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Ubaid told him, that Ali Ibn Abi Talib said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has forbidden you from eating the meat of your rituals for more than three nights.”"
"4396","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us of a recitation of it while I am listening and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that he informed him, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade eating meat.” The victims after three, then he said: “Eat, provide for yourself, and save.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4397","Issa bin Hammad Zaghbah told us, he said: Al-Layth informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Ibn Khabbab He is Abdullah bin Khabab. “Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri came from a journey, and his family brought him some of the meat of the sacrificial animals, so he said: I am not He ate it until he asked, so he went to his maternal brother Qatada bin Al-Numan, who was Badri, and asked him about that, and he said: It has happened. After you is an order that contradicts what they had previously forbidden of eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4398","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ishaq, he said: Zainab told me, she is Zainab bint Ka’b bin Ujrah. On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the meat of sacrificial animals for more than three days, so Qatada bin Al-Nu'man, who was Abu Sa'id's maternal brother and was Badri, so they came to him, and he said: Didn't the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid it? Abu Saeed said: Something happened about it, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from eating it for more than three days, then He gave us permission to eat it and store it.”"
"4399","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abdullah bin Muhammad, who is al-Nufayli, told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, and Muhammad bin Ma’dan told us. Bin Issa, he said: Al-Hasan bin Ayan told us, he said: Zuhayr told us, he said: Zubaid bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, I had forbidden you from visiting graves on three occasions, so visit them. May its visit increase you in goodness, and I forbade you from sacrificial meat after three days, so eat from it and abstain from what you wish, and I forbade you from drinks. In the vessels, so drink from any vessel you wish, and do not drink intoxicants, and abstain.” Muhammad did not mention: “And abstain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4400","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari informed us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas bin Jawab, on the authority of Ammar bin Ruzaiq, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zubayr. Ibn Adiy, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “I had forbidden you from sacrificial meat after... Three, and abstain from wine except as a drink, and abstain from visiting graves, so eat from the meat of the sacrificial animals as much as you wish, and provide for yourself and save, and whoever wants to visit graves, for they are a reminder of the Hereafter, and drink and beware of every intoxicant.”"
"4401","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Malik, he said: Abdullah bin Abi Bakr told me, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha said: “A group of people from the desert came in the presence of Eid al-Adha, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Eat and save three. After that, they said: O Messenger of God, the people were benefiting, that is, from their sacrificial animals, collecting donations from them, and taking Among them are watering things. He said: What is that? He said: You are forbidden from keeping the meat of sacrificial animals. He said: I only forbade the heater that warms them. Eat and save. And give charity.”"
"4402","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, he is Ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, he said: “ I went to Aisha and said: Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbid the meat of sacrificial animals after three days? She said: Yes, he did the same thing to the people Hardship, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, loved to feed the rich and the poor, then he said: I have seen the family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace. They eat the sheep after fifteen. I said: What is that? She laughed and said: The family of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, is never satisfied with unsweetened bread. Three days until he joined God Almighty.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4403","Yusuf bin Issa Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is the son of Ziyad bin Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abbas, on the authority of his father, said: I asked Aisha about sacrificial meat. She said: “We used to hide the livestock for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And he remained in peace for a month, then he would eat it.”"
"4404","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, informed us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Sa’id. Al-Khudri said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade keeping the sacrifice for more than three days, then he said: Eat and be fed.”"
"4405","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Al-Mughirah, he said: Humayd bin Hilal told us, he said: He told us Abdullah bin Mughaffal said, “A sack of fat was given to me on the Day of Khaybar, and I held it tight. I said, ‘I will not give any of it to anyone.’ Then I turned and saw the Messenger of God.” May God bless him and grant him peace, smiling.”"
"4406","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Nadhar bin Shumail told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, “ Some Bedouins were bringing meat to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Some Bedouins They bring us meat, and we do not know whether they mentioned the name of God over it or not. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Mention the name of God Almighty over it and eat."
"4407","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Harun bin Abi Waki’ told me, and he is Harun bin Antarah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “In His saying, the Mighty and Majestic, “And do not eat of that over which the name of God has not been mentioned.” He said: He opposed them. The polytheists, and they said: “Whatever God slaughters, do not eat, and whatever you slaughter, you may eat.”"
"4408","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Abu Tha’labah, he said: he said The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “It is not permissible to sit in a grave.”"
"4409","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hisham bin Zayd, he said: “I entered with Anas to rule, meaning Ibn Ayyub said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade animals to be stabbed.”"
"4410","Muhammad bin Zanbour al-Makki told us, saying: Ibn Abi Hazim told us, on the authority of Yazid, who is Ibn al-Hadi, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Abdullah Ibn Ja’far, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Ja’far, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by people who were shooting a ram with arrows, but he thought it disdain.” That said, “Do not imitate animals.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4411","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God was cursed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, whoever takes as an object something in which there is a soul.”"
"4412","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Al-Minhal bin Amr told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Umar said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “May God curse whoever mutilates an animal.”"
"4413","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Do not take anything in which there is a spirit” as an aim."
"4414","Muhammad bin Ubaid Al-Kufi told us, he said: Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Salih, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade taking anything that contains the spirit as an object.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4415","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Suhayb, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, he narrates it, he said He said: “Whoever kills a bird or something above it without its right, God Almighty will be asked about it on the Day of Resurrection. It was said: O Messenger of God, what is its right? He said: Her right is to slaughter it and eat it, and not to cut off its head and throw it away.”"
"4416","Muhammad bin Dawud al-Masisi told us, saying: Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, saying: Abu Ubaidah Abd al-Wahid bin Wasil told us, on the authority of Khalaf, meaning Ibn Mahran, said: Amer Al-Ahwal told us, on the authority of Salih bin Dinar, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Sharid, he said: I heard Al-Sharid, saying: I heard The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills a bird in vain will come to God Almighty on the Day of Resurrection, saying: O Lord, so-and-so killed me.” He did not kill me in vain, and he did not kill me for any gain.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4417","Othman bin Abdullah bin Kharzaz told me, he said: Sahl bin Bakkar told me, he said: Wahib bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his father, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr, he once said: on the authority of his father, and he once said: on the authority of his grandfather, On the Day of Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the meat of domestic donkeys, the jalala, the riding on them, and the eating of \her flesh\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4418","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Qatada told us, Ikrimah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade al-Mujathama, the milk of al-Jalala, and drinking from waterskins.”"
"4419","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Dawud bin Qais told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the Aqeeqah, and he said: God Almighty does not like disobedience, and it is as if he hated the name. He said to the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace: We only ask you about one of us who will have a child. He said: Whoever would like to keep you on behalf of his son, let him keep you on his behalf, on behalf of the boy. “Two fair sheep, and on behalf of the female slave, a sheep.” Dawud said: I asked Zaid bin Aslam about the two fair sheep. He said: The two suspicious sheep must be slaughtered. Everyone"
"4420","Al-Hussein bin Harith Abu Ammar told us, he said: Al-Fadl told us, he is Ibn Musa, on the authority of Al-Hussein bin Waqid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah. On the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the aqqa on behalf of Al-Hasan and Al-Husayn.”"
"4421","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ayyub, Habib, Yunus, and Qatada told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Salman bin Amer al-Dhabi, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is an aqeeqah on the boy, so shed blood on his behalf.” And remove the harm from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4422","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al-Zuhri told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Al-Rabab, on the authority of her uncle Salman. Bin Amer, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And the boy has an aqeeqah, so shed blood on his behalf, and remove the harm from him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4423","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid, on the authority of Umm Kurz, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “In the boy there are two reward sheep, and in the girl there is a sheep.”"
"4424","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Amr told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Habiba bint Maysarah, on the authority of Umm Karaz, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “For the boy, two fine sheep, and for the girl, a sheep.”"
"4425","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Abi Yazid, on the authority of Siba’ bin Thabit, on the authority of Umm Kurz, She said: “I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Al-Hudaybiyyah, asking him about sacrificial meat, and I heard him say: The boy has two sheep, and A female slave is a sheep. It will not harm you, whether male or female.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4426","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid told me, on the authority of Siba’ bin It is proven, on the authority of Umm Kurz, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Two sheep on behalf of the boy, and on the female slave a sheep, two males will not harm you. Or females?"
"4427","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim Ibn Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed aqaqah on the authority of Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God grant them two rams, two rams.”"
"4428","Amr bin Ali and Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala informed us, saying: Yazid, who is Ibn Zuray’, told us, on the authority of Saeed, he said: Qatada informed us, On the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “Every boy is pledged for his aqeeqah, which will be slaughtered for him on the day Seventh, his head shall be shaved, and his name shall be called \ (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4429","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Neither Fara’ nor Ataira”"
"4430","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I told Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Muammar and Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, one of them said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the branch And the 'Aitrah, and the other said: Neither Fara' nor 'Ateerah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4431","Amr bin Zurarah told us, he said: Muadh, who is Ibn Muadh, told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, he said: Abu Ramla told us, he said: he told us Mikhnaf bin Sulaym said: “While we were standing with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at Arafat, he said: “O people, there is a duty upon the family of every household.” “A year for the sacrifice of sacrifice and the month of ‘Aidarah.” Muadh said: Ibn Aoun used to sacrifice his sacrifice. My eyes saw him in Rajab. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4432","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub bin Ishaq told me, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Abdul Majeed Abu Ali al-Hanafi told us, he said: Dawud bin Qais told us, He said: I heard Amr bin Shuaib bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his father, and Zaid bin Aslam, they said: “Oh The Messenger of God, Al-Far’, said: It is true, so if you leave him until he is a virgin, then you carry a burden for him in the way of God, or give him a widow, that is better than that. You slaughter it, and its flesh sticks to its hair, so you fill your vessel and give it to your she-camel. They said: O Messenger of God, is the old woman real? He said: The old woman is real \"," (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4433","Suwayd bin Nasr informed us, saying: Abdullah, meaning Ibn Al-Mubarak, informed us on the authority of Yahya, who is Ibn Zurarah Ibn Karim Ibn Al-Harith bin Amr Al-Bahili said: I heard my father mentioning that he heard his grandfather Al-Harith bin Amr narrating, “He met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” Peace and blessings of God be upon him, during the Farewell Hajj while he was riding his lean camel, so I came to him from one of his two parts, and said: O Messenger of God, may my father be sacrificed for you. And my mother asked forgiveness for me, and he said: May God forgive you. Then I came to him from the other side, hoping that he would single me out over them, so I said: O Messenger of God, Ask forgiveness for me, so he said with his hand: May God forgive you, and a man from among the people said: O Messenger of God, the items and the offspring. He said: Whoever wishes, may he be freed, and whoever wishes will not. He may sacrifice, and whoever wishes may divide, and whoever wishes may not divide among the sacrificial sheep, and may clench his fingers except one.”"
"4434","Harun bin Abdullah told me, he said: Affan told us, he said: Yahya bin Zurarah al-Sahmi told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of his grandfather Al-Harith bin Amr. H And Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Hisham bin Abdul Malik Abu Al-Walid Al-Tayalisi told us, he said: Yahya bin Zurrah, who is the son of Karim bin Al-Harith Amr Al-Sahmi, said: My father told me, on the authority of his grandfather Al-Harith bin Amr, that he met the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, during the Farewell Pilgrimage, so I said: By my father’s ransom, O Messenger of God, ask forgiveness for me. He said: May God forgive you, while he was riding his camel. Al-Adaba, then I turned from the other side.” The hadith included"
"4435","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Jamil told us, on the authority of Abu al-Malih, on the authority of Nubaysha, He said: “It was mentioned to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: We used to sacrifice in pre-Islamic times. He said: Sacrifice to God Almighty in whatever month it is, and be righteous.” God Almighty, and feed them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4436","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, told us on the authority of Khalid, and he may have said: On the authority of Abu al-Malih, and he may have mentioned Abu Qalabah, on the authority of Nubaysha, said: “A man called out while he was in Mina and said: O Messenger of God, we used to mourn a woman in the pre-Islamic era in Rajab, but what Do you command us, O Messenger of God? He said: Sacrifice in any month, whatever it may be, and be righteous to God Almighty and feed. He said: We used to sacrifice a month, but what about? Do you command us? He said: In every wild animal there is a branch that you feed your livestock, until when it bears a lamb you slaughter it and give its meat in charity."
"4437","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, and I think I heard it from Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Nubaysha, a man from Hudhayl, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “I was I have forbidden you to eat more than three sacrificial meats in order to satisfy you, for God Almighty has brought goodness, so eat, give in charity, and save, and these are The days are days of eating and drinking, and he remembered God Almighty, and a man said: In the pre-Islamic era we used to observe the Ihrat prayer in Rajab, so what do you command us to do? He said: Sacrifice to God Almighty in whatever month it is, and honor God Almighty, and provide food. A man said: O Messenger of God, we used to sacrifice A branch in the pre-Islamic era. What do you command us to do? He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: In every flock of sheep there is a branch that your sheep feed on until then. “If you carry its slaughtered animal, and give its meat in charity to the wayfarer, for that is better.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4438","Abu Al-Ash’ath Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam and Muhammad bin Abdullah informed us, saying: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zuray’, he said: He informed us Khaled, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, on the authority of Nubaysha, said: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called a man and said: We were performing the Ihram at Mina in During the pre-Islamic era, in Rajab, what do you command us to do? He said: Slay them in whatever month it is, and be righteous to God Almighty, and feed them. He said: We used to give food. A branch in pre-Islamic times, he said: In every wild animal there is a branch, so when it bears a lamb you slaughter it and give its meat in charity, for that is better. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4439","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Abu Qalaba told me, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih, so I met Abu Al-Malih, so I asked him, and he told me, on the authority of Nubaysha Al-Hudhali. He said: “A man said: O Messenger of God, we used to observe the ‘itrah in pre-Islamic times, so what do you command us to do? He said: “Sacrifice to God Almighty in whatever month it is, and honor God Almighty and give food.”"
"4440","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Waki` bin Adas, on the authority of His uncle, Abu Razin Laqit bin Amir Al-Uqaili, said: “I said: O Messenger of God, we used to slaughter sacrifices in the pre-Islamic era in Rajab. So we eat and feed whoever comes to us, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no problem with him.” Waki’ bin Adas said: So I will not leave him."
"4441","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maimuna “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a dead sheep lying, and said: Who is this for? They said: For Maimouna, so he said: What is wrong with her if she benefits? By cutting it off? They said: It is dead. He said: God Almighty has only forbidden eating it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4442","Muhammad bin Salamah and Al-Harith bin Miskin told us of a recitation of it while I am listening and the pronunciation is his, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: He told me Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by with a sheep.” A dead animal that he had given to a servant of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Would you benefit from her skin? They said: O Messenger of God, It is dead, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God has only forbidden eating it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4443","Abd Al-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad told us, saying: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, on the authority of Ibn Abi Habib, meaning Yazid, on the authority of Hafs bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, narrated to him, that Ibn Abbas narrated to him, saying: “The Messenger of God saw God, may God bless him and grant him peace, a dead sheep belonging to an auspicious client, and it was a dead sheep in charity. He said: If they had removed its skin and benefited from it, they said: It is dead. He said: God has only forbidden eating it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4444","Abd al-Rahman bin Khalid al-Qattan al-Ruqqi told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Amr bin Dinar told me, he said: Ataa told me a while ago, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Maimunah told me, “A sheep died, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You took her hair and benefited from it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4445","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by He greeted a dead sheep from a young woman, and said: Did you not take its hide, tan it, and benefit from it? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4446","Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ash-Shabi, he said: Ibn Abbas said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by a sheep.” A dead woman, and he said: Did you not benefit from her slaughtering? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4447","Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rizmah informed us, saying: Al-Fadl bin Musa informed us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Sawda, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “A sheep died for us, so we tanned it.” He kept it, and we continued to reject it until it became a hardship.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4448","Qutayba bin Saeed and Ali bin Hajar informed us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Ibn Wa’ala, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Any cuticle that has been tanned has been purified.”"
"4449","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told me, he said: Ishaq bin Bakr, who is Ibn Mudar, told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah. He heard Abu Al-Khair, on the authority of Ibn Wa’ala, that he heard Ibn Abbas, and he said: “We are invading this Morocco, and they are People of an idol, and they have water bodies in which there are milk and water. Ibn Abbas said: Al-Dabbagh is pure. Ibn Wa’ala said: In your opinion or according to Did you hear anything from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Rather, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"4450","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of John bin Qatada, on the authority of Salamah ibn al-Muhabaq, “In the Battle of Tabuk, the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, called for water from a woman, and she said: What I have only a dead relative of mine. He said: Didn’t you tan it? She said: Yes. He said: For by tanning it, she killed it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4451","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Hussein Al-Marwazi bin Muhammad told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, On the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the skins of dead animals, and he said: tanning them.” \Her purity\"" (Peace Be Upon Him)"""
"4452","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: A partner told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad. On the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about the skins of a dead person, and he said: Tanning them is their slaughter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4453","Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan al-Ruqi told us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad told us, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The slaughter of a dead body is by tanning it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4454","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The slaughter of a dead body is by tanning it.”"
"4455","Suleiman bin Dawud informed us, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith and Al-Layth bin Saad informed me, on the authority of Kathir bin Farqad. Abdullah bin Malik bin Hudhafa narrated to him, on the authority of Al-Aliyah bint Subay’, that Maimuna was the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. She told her that men from the Quraysh passed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pulling a sheep for them like a donkey, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: May God bless him and grant him peace: If you had taken her hair! They said: It is dead, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Water and squirrels purify it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
